      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it signifies",
      "items": [
        "The pattern the series can explain using only its own past",
        "p, d, q = memory, differencing, shock memory",
        "Capital P, D, Q, s = the same three, repeated each season",
        "AIC balances fit quality against model complexity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Why it is used",
      "items": [
        "It has no external dependency, so it never breaks on a missing API",
        "It is the fair baseline SARIMAX must beat to justify macro drivers",
        "For a stable, seasonal market it is often the most reliable number",
        "The chosen order is a compact description of the series' behaviour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Read it this way",
      "items": [
        "Residual checks failing means real structure is still unmodelled",
        "Weekly with under 8 years skips seasonal AR/MA terms — the page says so",
        "AIC compares orders within this tab only, never across models",
        "If SARIMA beats SARIMAX, the macro drivers added nothing"
      ]
    }
